From 656b2c390535e3f5eb2a5ad31e5aa64c41e0f889 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:44:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] store: check the name after the rename or link of a temporary
 file

ReplaceFileIn, WriteFileAtomicIn and CreateFileAtomicIn look at the
name again with Root.Lstat after the rename or link: it must be a
regular file that os.SameFile takes for the temporary file written
(fstat on its descriptor; a duplicate of that descriptor keeps the
inode in use, so that its number is not given to another file).
Otherwise the error is the new store.ErrReplacedMeanwhile, and the
entry stays. Another process that put a directory under the temporary
name while witnesses.rec was missing made publish report success with
a directory under witnesses.rec (review of task 33 A, H1).

On every error the temporary name is removed only while it is still
the file written; an entry of another process stays, and the error is
ErrReplacedMeanwhile as well (review of task 34 A, N1). The name is
never opened again: a FIFO, a device or a socket under it neither
blocks nor is removed. The windows left (between the rename or link
and the Root.Lstat, and between the Root.Lstat and the unlink of the
temporary name) are named in the comments.

gomail-ceremony publish reports ErrReplacedMeanwhile with the path and
the remedy (stop the other process, look at platform/, run the same
publish again) and logs nothing; for witnesses.rec after the line of
WitnessesReplacing it says "is not the file publish wrote" when the
rename happened, "was not replaced" only when it failed (review of
task 34 A, N2), and calls no callback "replaced". A test build
(gomail_test) sets the hook of store for the tests of publish
(SetTempInHook).

Task: docs/tasks/33-nach-m1-nacht4.md (Paket 34A)
